    <fr:title text="A Grammar of Finite Cardinals">A Grammar of Finite Cardinals</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <fr:p>Define a grammar for each finite cardinal <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n : \mathbb {N}]]></fr:tex>.</fr:p>
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[ [0] \colonequals  \bot  ]]></fr:tex>
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[ [\mathsf {suc}(n)] \colonequals  \top  \oplus  [ n ]]]></fr:tex>
    <fr:p>Then define the grammar of all finite cardinals as
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathsf {Fin} \colonequals  \textstyle \mathchoice {\textstyle \oplus _{{\mathopen {}\left (n : \mathbb {N}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\textstyle \oplus _{{\mathopen {}\left (n : \mathbb {N}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptstyle \oplus _{{\mathopen {}\left (n : \mathbb {N}\right )\mathclose {}}}}{\scriptscriptstyle \oplus _{{\mathopen {}\left (n : \mathbb {N}\right )\mathclose {}}}}. [n]]]></fr:tex></fr:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
